#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# characteristic_polynomial

#% text
# `characteristic_polynomial(m, x)` gives the characteristic polynomial `det(x*I - m)` of the square matrix `m`, monic in `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The roots of the polynomial are the eigenvalues of `m`. Entries may be exact, symbolic or numerical.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
characteristic_polynomial([[1, 2], [3, 4]], x)
#% output
#= -2 - 5*x + x^2

#% cell
characteristic_polynomial([[a, b], [c, d]], x)
#% output
#= a*d - a*x - b*c - d*x + x^2

#% cell
characteristic_polynomial(identity_matrix(3), t)
#% output
#= -1 + 3*t - 3*t^2 + t^3

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The roots are the eigenvalues:

#% cell
m = [[2, 1], [1, 2]]; [solve(characteristic_polynomial(m, x) == 0, x), eigenvalues(m)]
#% output
#= [[[x -> 1], [x -> 3]], [3, 1]]

#% text
# Cayley-Hamilton: the matrix satisfies its own polynomial:

#% cell
m = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]; dot(m, m) - 5*m - 2*identity_matrix(2)
#% output
#= [[0, 0], [0, 0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `eigenvalues`, `det`, `trace`
